WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:27.547
<i>I remember very little from when
I still went to school.</i>

3
00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:30.049
<i>but there's one day I'll never forget:</i>

4
00:01:30.258 --> 00:01:32.635
<i>My first natural history class.</i>

5
00:01:33.469 --> 00:01:37.181
<i>The teacher was trying to explain
what a natural constant is.</i>

6
00:01:37.682 --> 00:01:40.434
<i>Something that. whatever happens.
will never change.</i>

7
00:01:41.435 --> 00:01:44.730
<i>He gave all kinds of examples
of natural constants:</i>

8
00:01:45.273 --> 00:01:49.110
<i>The passage of time. the tides.
the expansion of the universe.</i>

9
00:01:49.193 --> 00:01:54.240
<i>birth. death. gravity.
the contradiction of human nature.</i>

10
00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:56.993
<i>the change from day to night.
and night to day.</i>

11
00:01:57.076 --> 00:02:00.621
<i>photosynthesis in plants
and many more.</i>

12
00:02:01.122 --> 00:02:03.749
<i>Very excited with all these new terms.</i>

13
00:02:03.791 --> 00:02:05.877
<i>I got home at night. eager
to tell my father.</i>

14
00:02:06.586 --> 00:02:09.046
<i>but of course. my dad wasn't impressed.</i>

15
00:02:09.797 --> 00:02:11.674
<i>My dad has always been very smart.</i>

16
00:02:11.924 --> 00:02:14.302
<i>I think he's the
smartest person I've ever met.</i>

17
00:02:15.344 --> 00:02:19.557
<i>He just answered that. for him.
there were only two true constants:</i>

18
00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:22.392
<i>Family and change.</i>

19
00:02:23.436 --> 00:02:25.354
<i>I didn't understand
what he meant that night.</i>

20
00:02:25.938 --> 00:02:28.649
<i>I didn't understand
what he meant for a long time</i>

21
00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:06.646
How long?

22
00:03:06.896 --> 00:03:07.980
17 seconds.

23
00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:10.106
I won! I beat you.

24
00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:11.609
- Your turn.
- No. it's freezing!

25
00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.402
I'm the king of the lagoon.

26
00:03:14.487 --> 00:03:16.072
Oliver. no.

27
00:03:16.531 --> 00:03:18.407
Come on. jump in.

28
00:03:19.325 --> 00:03:20.952
No. I'm scared.

29
00:03:21.452 --> 00:03:23.692
But there's nothing Benja. don't worry.
Trust me. get in.

30
00:03:24.038 --> 00:03:26.666
I'm just scared. it looks too deep.

31
00:05:24.492 --> 00:05:26.077
What are you going to name that frog?

32
00:05:27.203 --> 00:05:29.121
Um. "Manchitas"

33
00:05:29.664 --> 00:05:31.541
Because of the spots on her back.

34
00:05:31.582 --> 00:05:34.544
No! Name her Kermit. like Kermit the Frog.

35
00:05:36.838 --> 00:05:38.965
Is Pink going to be jealous?

36
00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.217
I don't think so.

37
00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.261
She's been feeling very lonely.

38
00:05:43.594 --> 00:05:45.555
Who is Kermit the Frog?

39
00:06:11.205 --> 00:06:12.874
Salvador.

40
00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:16.127
Chava

41
00:06:16.377 --> 00:06:17.795
Don't call me that!

42
00:06:18.212 --> 00:06:19.380
What do you want?

43
00:06:20.256 --> 00:06:21.591
Bring Guillermina.

44
00:06:46.741 --> 00:06:47.825
What took you so long?

45
00:06:47.909 --> 00:06:49.494
Uh. Asshole!

46
00:06:49.535 --> 00:06:51.162
What happened to your face?

47
00:06:52.205 --> 00:06:53.414
Camouflage.

48
00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:57.877
It's big.

49
00:06:57.919 --> 00:06:59.128
Also far.

50
00:06:59.921 --> 00:07:01.464
Not for Guille.

51
00:07:03.925 --> 00:07:06.135
Go. watch out.

52
00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.111
Hello little dog.

53
00:07:24.904 --> 00:07:25.904
Come little dog.

54
00:07:26.697 --> 00:07:27.697
Come.

55
00:07:28.366 --> 00:07:29.408
Doggy. come here.

56
00:07:31.869 --> 00:07:32.869
That's it!

57
00:07:57.061 --> 00:07:59.272
Are the monster's teeth like these?

58
00:07:59.313 --> 00:08:01.106
Hey! Don't touch that!

59
00:08:01.107 --> 00:08:02.441
No. they are much worse.

60
00:08:02.483 --> 00:08:05.444
Those are not teeth. those are fangs.
they can kill you with one bite.

61
00:08:11.075 --> 00:08:12.410
What's that?

62
00:08:15.037 --> 00:08:16.372
It’s my pet.

63
00:08:16.455 --> 00:08:18.166
- Another one?
- It's ours.

64
00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:21.002
You didn't find more?

65
00:08:21.085 --> 00:08:24.005
- It's called "Manchitas".
- No. it's called Kermit.

66
00:08:24.422 --> 00:08:26.132
Can we make a little house for it?

67
00:08:27.216 --> 00:08:28.342
No problem.

68
00:08:28.384 --> 00:08:29.635
I'll take care of it.

69
00:09:14.347 --> 00:09:15.597
Did you come down yesterday?

70
00:09:15.598 --> 00:09:16.349
No.

71
00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:17.850
Two days without noise.

72
00:09:21.062 --> 00:09:22.063
Are you hungry?

73
00:09:25.024 --> 00:09:27.360
Yes. A little.

74
00:09:30.822 --> 00:09:33.449
Go with Benjamin.
I'll let you know in a while.

75
00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:52.844
Smells good. what is it?

76
00:09:52.885 --> 00:09:53.885
Protein.

77
00:10:09.318 --> 00:10:10.862
What did you put in it?

78
00:10:11.529 --> 00:10:12.572
The...

79
00:10:12.905 --> 00:10:14.115
The frog?

80
00:10:18.327 --> 00:10:19.370
Manchitas?

81
00:10:24.167 --> 00:10:26.669
You promised
to take care of her!

82
00:10:27.461 --> 00:10:28.921
Benny. understand we have to eat.

83
00:10:28.963 --> 00:10:30.089
She was mine!

84
00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:34.843
When my parents come home
I'll tell them you killed my frog!

85
00:10:34.844 --> 00:10:35.969
Please. sit down and eat!

86
00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:37.722
I don't want anything!
I don't want to eat!

87
00:10:38.014 --> 00:10:40.266
You are the worst brother in the world!

88
00:10:40.766 --> 00:10:41.851
You are poop!

89
00:10:41.893 --> 00:10:43.144
Poop! You hear me?

90
00:10:43.352 --> 00:10:44.353
Poop!

91
00:10:44.395 --> 00:10:45.813
I said sit down!

92
00:10:48.608 --> 00:10:50.735
We eat what we have. dumb head!

93
00:10:51.068 --> 00:10:53.905
That frog is better on your plate
than in that damn jar over there!

94
00:10:54.655 --> 00:10:56.781
But if you don't want it. I will eat it.

95
00:10:56.782 --> 00:10:58.284
I won't eat it!

96
00:11:03.456 --> 00:11:05.624
Why don't you get like this
when we kill the dogs?

97
00:11:05.625 --> 00:11:08.127
That has nothing to do with this!

98
00:11:08.419 --> 00:11:10.630
The dogs are for him!

99
00:11:11.547 --> 00:11:13.591
Manchitas was mine!

100
00:11:13.841 --> 00:11:15.009
She was mine!

101
00:11:15.176 --> 00:11:18.304
It was so Pink
wouldn't feel so lonely!

102
00:11:38.741 --> 00:11:40.576
Did you finish with the dishes?

103
00:11:41.118 --> 00:11:42.119
Yes.

104
00:11:43.287 --> 00:11:44.622
Benjamin cries about everything.

105
00:11:44.789 --> 00:11:47.834
I have a crybaby and a coward.
I'm screwed.

106
00:11:48.626 --> 00:11:52.630
Come on. he is seven.
Give him a break. he misses mom and dad.

107
00:11:54.298 --> 00:11:58.553
Well. I also miss many things.
but here I am busting my ass. you see?

108
00:12:04.308 --> 00:12:06.519
Benjamin! Go with him right now!

109
00:12:07.478 --> 00:12:08.521
Let's go upstairs!

110
00:12:08.563 --> 00:12:09.814
Quickly Benjamin!

111
00:12:13.317 --> 00:12:14.485
Get down!

112
00:12:15.027 --> 00:12:16.195
Run!

113
00:12:24.328 --> 00:12:25.538
Everything will be alright.

114
00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:28.166
We'll take care of it!
Don't come out. okay?

115
00:14:45.428 --> 00:14:47.346
Why the fuck don't you knock?

116
00:14:50.516 --> 00:14:52.643
One of the hanged fell.

117
00:15:07.825 --> 00:15:09.494
One. two. three.

118
00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:12.747
Benja. how’s that knot going?

119
00:15:12.788 --> 00:15:14.540
One. two. three.

120
00:15:15.583 --> 00:15:17.627
Help him tie that knot. Run!

121
00:15:18.085 --> 00:15:19.337
One. two. three.

122
00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.767
Can't you tie a fucking knot?

123
00:15:33.351 --> 00:15:34.769
Of course we can. Look!

124
00:15:49.367 --> 00:15:56.582
PÁRVULOS

125
00:17:27.048 --> 00:17:29.050
Still not growing. Shit!

126
00:17:33.346 --> 00:17:35.932
I told you this was my lucky stick.

127
00:17:36.014 --> 00:17:38.559
I'll hit the monster
if he breaks free.

128
00:17:38.768 --> 00:17:42.061
Benja. your stick is useless
against the monster.

129
00:17:42.062 --> 00:17:44.023
If he sees you
he will swallow you in one bite.

130
00:17:44.065 --> 00:17:45.525
What if I put it in his mouth?

131
00:17:45.566 --> 00:17:47.068
It breaks in a second.

132
00:17:47.151 --> 00:17:48.277
Rake. please!

133
00:17:48.361 --> 00:17:49.904
What if I stuck it in his eye?

134
00:17:49.987 --> 00:17:51.823
It will just get angrier.

135
00:17:51.864 --> 00:17:52.865
Rake!

136
00:17:53.115 --> 00:17:55.493
His senses are more developed than ours.

137
00:17:55.701 --> 00:17:58.120
Rake. damn it!
Can't you hear me?

138
00:17:58.621 --> 00:17:59.913
Cut out the weeds.

139
00:17:59.914 --> 00:18:02.750
get water from the pond.
also compost.

140
00:19:10.109 --> 00:19:12.111
Hey! What's wrong with you?
It was about to end.

141
00:19:12.153 --> 00:19:14.822
Aren’t you sick of watching
the same damn movie?

142
00:19:16.574 --> 00:19:18.408
We need to set more bird traps.

143
00:19:18.409 --> 00:19:20.244
We haven't caught anything in weeks.

144
00:19:20.453 --> 00:19:23.414
Well. then we need to use more
plant fertilizer.

145
00:19:23.623 --> 00:19:25.333
We do that. And meanwhile?

146
00:19:25.416 --> 00:19:28.044
You can't keep risking him like this.
It's dangerous for him.

147
00:19:28.085 --> 00:19:29.462
It's dangerous for both of us.

148
00:19:29.545 --> 00:19:31.087
Then don't go!

149
00:19:31.088 --> 00:19:34.300
I don't want to expose him.
but I can't go alone nor stay alone.

150
00:19:34.842 --> 00:19:37.720
One of us has to stay here
and take food to the basement.

151
00:19:37.803 --> 00:19:39.555
Should we leave him or what?

152
00:19:40.097 --> 00:19:41.307
Salvador

153
00:19:41.557 --> 00:19:42.850
I can't sleep.

154
00:19:43.476 --> 00:19:44.894
I'm scared.

155
00:19:46.687 --> 00:19:51.067
“At first. the father was utterly opposed
to the idea of leaving his children

156
00:19:51.108 --> 00:19:52.944
at the mercy of the forest”.

157
00:19:53.152 --> 00:19:55.321
“How can you even say that. woman?”

158
00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:57.656
“What kind of father do you think I am?

159
00:19:57.657 --> 00:19:59.242
He replied angrily.”

160
00:19:59.575 --> 00:20:02.537
“The woman. who was keen to get
rid of the burden of the children.

161
00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:05.121
did not rest until she convinced
the weak lumberjack

162
00:20:05.122 --> 00:20:08.876
that this was
the only thing they could do”.

163
00:20:12.046 --> 00:20:14.506
“The children were not really asleep.

164
00:20:14.507 --> 00:20:18.052
so they heard the whole conversation
by their door”.

165
00:20:18.094 --> 00:20:19.594
“The next morning.

166
00:20:19.595 --> 00:20:22.514
the children followed their father
deep into the forest”.

167
00:20:22.515 --> 00:20:25.767
“Hansel trailed behind.
dropping breadcrumbs

168
00:20:25.768 --> 00:20:29.355
to mark the path that would
take them back home”.

169
00:20:30.231 --> 00:20:32.441
- “We have to go to the forest”...
- I think he’s asleep.

170
00:20:45.413 --> 00:20:48.416
Do you think the monster ate our parents?

171
00:20:49.417 --> 00:20:51.335
No. Benjamin. how can you say that?

172
00:20:51.794 --> 00:20:53.671
Then. why haven't they come back?

173
00:20:54.297 --> 00:20:56.465
Have they forgotten we're here?

174
00:20:57.758 --> 00:21:01.262
What if they caught the virus and
don't have the vaccine?

175
00:21:01.596 --> 00:21:02.847
No. of course not.

176
00:21:03.014 --> 00:21:06.057
That's from the old world.
You've better go to sleep

177
00:21:06.058 --> 00:21:07.852
we're leaving early in the morning.

178
00:22:06.244 --> 00:22:08.496
Benjamin! What the hell are you doing?

179
00:22:08.663 --> 00:22:10.248
Are you a fucking idiot or what?

180
00:22:11.207 --> 00:22:12.959
You know you can’t go in
the basement!

181
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.293
Do you want to die?

182
00:22:14.335 --> 00:22:16.212
When will you let me see it?

183
00:22:16.337 --> 00:22:18.130
Not until you’re 10!

184
00:22:18.214 --> 00:22:20.715
Oliver saw it before he was 10!

185
00:22:20.716 --> 00:22:23.135
If you get distracted
it will kill you in one bite.

186
00:22:23.177 --> 00:22:24.178
don't you get it?

187
00:22:32.812 --> 00:22:34.355
We have to work together. Benja.

188
00:22:35.273 --> 00:22:36.566
No room for kids here.

189
00:22:37.024 --> 00:22:39.735
I'm bigger but you have two legs.
we're equal.

190
00:22:40.528 --> 00:22:41.696
We have to find some food.

191
00:22:41.737 --> 00:22:43.071
Grab your stuff.

192
00:22:43.072 --> 00:22:44.115
Let's go.

193
00:23:02.508 --> 00:23:04.051
Please. don't go!

194
00:24:34.350 --> 00:24:36.686
The pandemic came this far?

195
00:24:37.562 --> 00:24:40.022
It reached the entire world.
but that wasn't the problem.

196
00:24:44.861 --> 00:24:45.903
Let's go.

197
00:25:14.891 --> 00:25:15.933
Let's go.

198
00:25:54.764 --> 00:25:55.932
Don't go too far away.

199
00:26:14.992 --> 00:26:16.911
Look what I found!

200
00:27:48.044 --> 00:27:49.628
No. no. no. don't come up here!

201
00:27:49.629 --> 00:27:50.796
There's nothing to see here.

202
00:28:12.902 --> 00:28:15.780
What if we moved to the abandoned house?

203
00:28:15.822 --> 00:28:18.699
So each of us could have his own room.

204
00:28:19.826 --> 00:28:21.035
What about the monster?

205
00:28:21.452 --> 00:28:23.162
Why do you care so much for it?

206
00:28:25.039 --> 00:28:26.457
We can't let it starve to death.

207
00:28:27.041 --> 00:28:28.376
We are not like that.

208
00:28:29.001 --> 00:28:33.047
After all. it's like an animal.
like your frog. also like Pink.

209
00:28:34.215 --> 00:28:36.884
We found it and now
we have to take care of it.

210
00:28:37.677 --> 00:28:39.636
Besides.
if mom and dad come back

211
00:28:39.637 --> 00:28:42.139
and don't see us.
they'll think something happened to us.

212
00:28:44.934 --> 00:28:47.520
Chava. do you miss it?

213
00:28:48.146 --> 00:28:49.313
Miss what?

214
00:28:49.397 --> 00:28:51.440
Well. everything. as it was before.

215
00:28:52.817 --> 00:28:55.236
Sometimes. when I get bored.

216
00:28:56.070 --> 00:28:57.822
And when you're not?

217
00:29:01.742 --> 00:29:03.076
What about you?

218
00:29:03.077 --> 00:29:04.162
Do you miss anything?

219
00:29:05.288 --> 00:29:08.541
Mmm. Dad used to snore very loudly.

220
00:29:08.708 --> 00:29:09.876
Like this. look!

221
00:29:12.420 --> 00:29:13.671
That would wake me up.

222
00:29:14.088 --> 00:29:18.134
I also miss mom's pancakes
with apple and pecans.

223
00:29:20.928 --> 00:29:22.471
Pancake Saturdays.

224
00:29:27.560 --> 00:29:30.229
They'll surely be back
for Christmas. right?

225
00:29:33.816 --> 00:29:35.610
The trumpets passed through here.

226
00:29:35.693 --> 00:29:38.404
It was just one body. but they
took out his hearth and everything.

227
00:29:39.238 --> 00:29:40.573
When are you coming back?

228
00:29:42.116 --> 00:29:43.784
We have to go around.

229
00:29:43.910 --> 00:29:46.496
I can't go up the hill
with all this stuff.

230
00:29:47.121 --> 00:29:48.664
Today it jumped at me!

231
00:29:49.624 --> 00:29:50.666
It almost got me!

232
00:29:53.377 --> 00:29:55.505
Benja asked why
we can't leave the house.

233
00:29:56.797 --> 00:29:57.924
What did you say?

234
00:29:58.299 --> 00:30:00.426
Well. nothing.
What am I going to say?

235
00:30:00.468 --> 00:30:03.137
Well. the truth.
he understands more than you think.

236
00:30:05.890 --> 00:30:07.141
You still have dog?

237
00:30:07.683 --> 00:30:09.310
If it's over before we get back...

238
00:30:09.352 --> 00:30:10.936
Well. yes. I know.

239
00:30:10.937 --> 00:30:12.522
You don't have to remind me.

240
00:30:15.566 --> 00:30:16.567
Good night. Oliver.

241
00:30:17.902 --> 00:30:18.985
Good night.

242
00:30:18.986 --> 00:30:20.279
Over and out.

243
00:30:44.053 --> 00:30:45.721
Rest stop.

244
00:30:58.901 --> 00:31:00.236
Does it hurt?

245
00:31:01.529 --> 00:31:02.864
Only when I laugh.

246
00:31:05.032 --> 00:31:06.868
I'm going to the river to fill the canteen.

247
00:31:07.785 --> 00:31:09.120
It's loaded. okay?

248
00:31:09.871 --> 00:31:11.247
Be careful.

249
00:31:16.919 --> 00:31:18.421
Don't move from here.

250
00:32:24.153 --> 00:32:25.154
No!

251
00:32:32.745 --> 00:32:34.288
Let's go. let's go!

252
00:32:35.706 --> 00:32:36.707
Where is the backpack?

253
00:32:36.749 --> 00:32:39.085
Run! Grab your bike. let's go!

254
00:33:10.032 --> 00:33:12.160
Salvador. Benny.

255
00:33:13.119 --> 00:33:14.287
Pick up.

256
00:33:14.620 --> 00:33:16.038
Pick up. dammit!

257
00:33:20.001 --> 00:33:22.128
I don't want to be here alone.

258
00:33:25.214 --> 00:33:28.217
Salvador. Benny? Pick up!

259
00:33:29.010 --> 00:33:31.387
Just tell me you're okay!

260
00:34:11.052 --> 00:34:12.762
Why didn't you answer?

261
00:34:14.305 --> 00:34:16.682
Heat up water for a bath. run.

262
00:34:19.685 --> 00:34:22.563
I lost the radio.
The backpack fell into the river.

263
00:34:24.190 --> 00:34:25.274
I fucked up.

264
00:36:11.756 --> 00:36:12.965
Let me go!

265
00:36:14.550 --> 00:36:16.511
Help. help!

266
00:36:21.724 --> 00:36:22.725
Let's go Benjamin!

267
00:36:31.943 --> 00:36:34.362
Omega-virus. that's what they called it.

268
00:36:35.071 --> 00:36:37.490
Many years ago. before you were born.

269
00:36:37.740 --> 00:36:39.367
another virus stopped this world.

270
00:36:39.784 --> 00:36:42.662
Not what you saw in mom and dad.
Something else.

271
00:36:43.079 --> 00:36:44.372
The pandemic?

272
00:36:44.789 --> 00:36:46.332
It was also very hard.

273
00:36:47.124 --> 00:36:49.961
People could not go out
and live their lives.

274
00:36:50.628 --> 00:36:51.921
The economy collapsed.

275
00:36:52.880 --> 00:36:55.550
I don't know what that is
but that's what I've been told.

276
00:36:56.259 --> 00:36:59.303
Humanity was in urgent
and desperate need for a vaccine.

277
00:36:59.679 --> 00:37:01.805
They were vaccinated
with whatever they could find.

278
00:37:01.806 --> 00:37:04.976
At first everything was going well.
but then

279
00:37:05.017 --> 00:37:08.396
the virus kept mutating.
they kept updating the vaccines.

280
00:37:08.813 --> 00:37:11.983
at some point. the virus mutated
faster than the vaccines.

281
00:37:12.191 --> 00:37:14.944
They had to administer a vaccine
that was not well tested. so...

282
00:37:16.112 --> 00:37:19.115
the Omega
was one of the side effects.

283
00:37:20.032 --> 00:37:23.744
It is believed that 83 percent of people
already have omega.

284
00:37:23.995 --> 00:37:25.329
Will they die?

285
00:37:27.165 --> 00:37:28.166
Benja!

286
00:37:28.624 --> 00:37:31.752
You don't know how surprised
I am that they’re not dead already.

287
00:37:33.129 --> 00:37:35.673
So. those screams at night are...

288
00:37:35.715 --> 00:37:36.924
It's them.

289
00:37:38.426 --> 00:37:41.095
Sometimes they fight
because dad wants to...

290
00:37:41.262 --> 00:37:42.262
Eat?

291
00:37:43.806 --> 00:37:44.807
No.

292
00:37:45.349 --> 00:37:46.434
Ride.

293
00:37:51.063 --> 00:37:52.648
I don't want them to die!

294
00:37:52.857 --> 00:37:54.317
I want them to be cured!

295
00:37:54.358 --> 00:37:57.820
So do we Benja.
but there is no cure.

296
00:37:58.446 --> 00:38:00.781
Then why do you have them locked up?

297
00:38:00.865 --> 00:38:04.494
I believe there is a cure.
it must exist or they will discover it.

298
00:38:05.036 --> 00:38:06.621
We just have to be patient.

299
00:38:07.163 --> 00:38:08.873
The world is fucked up.

300
00:38:09.415 --> 00:38:11.918
Tell me who the hell
is going to discover it?

301
00:38:13.252 --> 00:38:16.589
Mom and dad took care of us
when the omega started.

302
00:38:17.298 --> 00:38:18.716
They took us out of the city.

303
00:38:19.091 --> 00:38:21.719
We couldn't live there.
it was very dangerous.

304
00:38:22.261 --> 00:38:24.180
We were wandering for a long time.

305
00:38:24.222 --> 00:38:26.641
Then we found this house
and everything changed.

306
00:38:27.642 --> 00:38:31.020
They taught us everything
we needed to survive.

307
00:38:32.438 --> 00:38:33.606
Until...

308
00:38:33.773 --> 00:38:34.357
No.

309
00:38:34.482 --> 00:38:38.736
Well. something good is
going to come out of this.

310
00:38:40.029 --> 00:38:41.113
Benja...

311
00:38:41.656 --> 00:38:43.416
We don't have to hide
them from you anymore.

312
00:38:44.116 --> 00:38:46.661
You are a big boy now.
You know the truth.

313
00:38:46.953 --> 00:38:49.747
Now you will help us take care of them.

314
00:38:56.462 --> 00:38:58.631
Calm down mom.
it’s just your sunglasses.

315
00:39:03.845 --> 00:39:05.513
Ready? Let's go!

316
00:39:14.772 --> 00:39:15.773
Hey. hey.

317
00:39:16.149 --> 00:39:17.358
Give her a chance.

318
00:39:17.400 --> 00:39:19.193
It's been ages since she came out.

319
00:39:22.446 --> 00:39:24.740
Fresh air. mom! And some sun!

320
00:39:25.199 --> 00:39:27.118
Hey! No biting!

321
00:39:33.416 --> 00:39:35.835
Look mom. it’s the wilderness.

322
00:39:35.877 --> 00:39:37.295
These are trees.

323
00:39:38.004 --> 00:39:42.216
I tried to paint them when I was little.
but they came out all wrong.

324
00:39:42.383 --> 00:39:47.138
The teacher told me
they were too thin and all crooked.

325
00:39:48.806 --> 00:39:53.227
One day.
you and dad took me to see them.

326
00:39:53.936 --> 00:39:55.480
I can still remember.

327
00:39:56.856 --> 00:39:58.941
Look mom. touch them.

328
00:39:59.942 --> 00:40:03.112
Benja. you have to understand.
Mom is not what she used to be.

329
00:40:03.571 --> 00:40:04.614
She can't understand you.

330
00:40:04.697 --> 00:40:06.491
I know she understands me.

331
00:40:06.949 --> 00:40:08.034
Look mom.

332
00:40:09.785 --> 00:40:12.747
Touch them. feel them.

333
00:40:13.789 --> 00:40:16.083
Feel them. they are trees.

334
00:40:23.925 --> 00:40:25.510
See. I told you.

335
00:40:27.136 --> 00:40:29.347
Keep a tight grip.
I don't like this.

336
00:40:29.430 --> 00:40:30.556
We need to go back.

337
00:40:30.598 --> 00:40:32.141
Can’t leave dad alone for so long.

338
00:40:32.475 --> 00:40:34.101
I know they can change.

339
00:40:34.602 --> 00:40:36.938
They can remember who they were before.

340
00:40:37.772 --> 00:40:40.358
Trust me. we're going to train them.

341
00:41:22.441 --> 00:41:27.071
Let me train them for a few days.
You'll see I'm right.

342
00:41:41.085 --> 00:41:42.670
Let's go Benja. is late.

343
00:41:43.004 --> 00:41:44.589
I know it's been a hard day for you.

344
00:41:44.672 --> 00:41:47.008
- I don't want to go!
- Benja let's go!

345
00:41:47.091 --> 00:41:48.342
- No!
- Listen to me!

346
00:42:25.463 --> 00:42:26.631
Benja. go to bed.

347
00:42:27.757 --> 00:42:29.175
Benja. it's really late.

348
00:42:30.676 --> 00:42:32.220
Tomorrow will be a long day.

349
00:44:54.445 --> 00:44:55.446
Sit down.

350
00:44:56.155 --> 00:44:57.156
Sit down.

351
00:44:58.533 --> 00:44:59.534
Sit down!

352
00:45:30.481 --> 00:45:31.482
Go away. go away!

353
00:45:31.649 --> 00:45:32.775
I'm OK. I'm OK.

354
00:46:02.221 --> 00:46:03.806
We're not going to chain them?

355
00:46:04.182 --> 00:46:05.433
I don't think so.

356
00:46:05.475 --> 00:46:06.893
They've earned it.

357
00:46:07.101 --> 00:46:09.145
Benja. you were right.

358
00:46:09.896 --> 00:46:11.481
They are improving.

359
00:46:11.939 --> 00:46:13.774
I want to try something.

360
00:46:17.153 --> 00:46:18.154
Look mom.

361
00:46:22.158 --> 00:46:23.576
Say horse.

362
00:46:24.785 --> 00:46:26.162
Say horse.

363
00:46:28.623 --> 00:46:30.583
Horse.

364
00:46:31.918 --> 00:46:33.211
Say it mom.

365
00:46:35.588 --> 00:46:37.840
Look mom. it's a pig.

366
00:46:38.549 --> 00:46:39.592
Say pig.

367
00:46:40.468 --> 00:46:42.220
- Pig.
- Benja.

368
00:46:42.678 --> 00:46:44.722
We have made progress.
but let’s keep it real.

369
00:46:44.972 --> 00:46:46.557
They will never be like before.

370
00:46:46.933 --> 00:46:50.061
What? You just said I was right.

371
00:46:50.144 --> 00:46:52.730
Benja. understand.
we can train them a bit.

372
00:46:53.397 --> 00:46:56.609
but you won't make them talk.
or remind them of who you are.

373
00:46:56.734 --> 00:46:57.777
Anyway.

374
00:46:58.027 --> 00:47:00.238
I think it's time for them to have dinner.
Oliver.

375
00:47:16.254 --> 00:47:17.505
That's gross!

376
00:47:19.173 --> 00:47:21.425
Why do they like to eat that?

377
00:47:21.676 --> 00:47:24.512
I don't know if they like it. but
they eat it and that is enough.

378
00:47:24.804 --> 00:47:26.055
"Pig"

379
00:47:26.973 --> 00:47:28.099
"Pig"

380
00:47:28.891 --> 00:47:30.017
She spoke!

381
00:47:31.352 --> 00:47:34.605
Pig. Do you remember food. mom?

382
00:47:35.982 --> 00:47:37.817
- Food.
- Ham. sausage.

383
00:47:37.859 --> 00:47:39.277
Do you remember. mom?

384
00:47:40.820 --> 00:47:43.656
Speaking of dinner. tomorrow is Christmas.

385
00:47:43.865 --> 00:47:48.035
I know there won't be any gifts.
or visits from Santa. but...

386
00:47:48.661 --> 00:47:51.289
We're having a special dinner
like last year. right?

387
00:47:51.455 --> 00:47:52.622
Don't even think about it.

388
00:47:52.623 --> 00:47:55.459
You said they no longer had
to be chained.

389
00:47:55.626 --> 00:47:56.961
We're just testing!

390
00:47:57.211 --> 00:47:58.462
Oliver. help me.

391
00:47:58.629 --> 00:47:59.672
He's right. Salvador.

392
00:48:00.173 --> 00:48:02.091
We have made giant steps these days.

393
00:48:02.258 --> 00:48:04.385
We barely have food for ourselves.

394
00:48:04.468 --> 00:48:05.595
You said it yourself.

395
00:48:05.636 --> 00:48:07.680
They’ll be happy with a couple of rats.

396
00:48:14.187 --> 00:48:15.188
Pig.

397
00:48:19.984 --> 00:48:22.527
Hello to my beloved audience!

398
00:48:22.528 --> 00:48:25.865
Tonight is a very special night.

399
00:48:26.073 --> 00:48:28.451
That’s why I'm going to sing

400
00:48:28.493 --> 00:48:32.788
my Christmas carols!

401
00:48:38.085 --> 00:48:40.338
Christmas is here.
Time for merriment and cheer.

402
00:48:40.505 --> 00:48:43.174
With mom and dad today.
we're going to celebrate.

403
00:48:43.299 --> 00:48:44.299
Christmas is here.

404
00:48:44.300 --> 00:48:45.635
Time for merriment and cheer.

405
00:48:45.718 --> 00:48:47.970
With mom and dad today.
we're going to celebrate.

406
00:48:52.642 --> 00:48:54.935
Christmas is here. everything is neat.

407
00:48:54.936 --> 00:48:57.230
Finally. tonight my family is complete.

408
00:48:57.480 --> 00:48:59.649
Christmas is here. everything is neat.

409
00:48:59.690 --> 00:49:04.111
Finally. tonight my family is complete!

410
00:49:04.821 --> 00:49:07.365
Thank you. beautiful crowd!

411
00:49:07.573 --> 00:49:08.741
Thank you.

412
00:49:15.623 --> 00:49:17.208
A little closer. Benja.

413
00:49:17.250 --> 00:49:19.043
Smile. Oliver.

414
00:49:20.044 --> 00:49:21.254
Ready?

415
00:49:49.949 --> 00:49:51.075
Let me see.

416
00:49:52.869 --> 00:49:54.244
Can I see?

417
00:49:54.245 --> 00:49:55.371
I want to see it.

418
00:50:07.008 --> 00:50:08.050
Look dad.

419
00:50:08.676 --> 00:50:11.846
Look dad. dad. look at the photo.

420
00:50:12.763 --> 00:50:13.848
The photo.

421
00:50:15.266 --> 00:50:16.267
Look.

422
00:50:21.731 --> 00:50:23.191
Look mom.

423
00:50:24.650 --> 00:50:25.651
Look.

424
00:50:25.776 --> 00:50:29.405
This is dad. this is Salvador.

425
00:50:29.447 --> 00:50:33.117
This is Oliver. this is me.

426
00:50:33.784 --> 00:50:35.244
This is you.

427
00:50:38.372 --> 00:50:39.957
She does recognize us!

428
00:50:41.209 --> 00:50:42.293
She recognizes herself!

429
00:50:42.460 --> 00:50:44.629
She doesn't like it!
Oliver take the muzzles. quick!

430
00:50:44.670 --> 00:50:46.130
Ah!

431
00:51:23.835 --> 00:51:25.127
Benjamin. what are you doing?

432
00:51:25.336 --> 00:51:27.672
I want to teach them to eat real food.

433
00:51:30.424 --> 00:51:32.426
Put on your helmet. be careful.

434
00:51:38.975 --> 00:51:39.976
Look. mommy.

435
00:51:40.184 --> 00:51:42.019
It's soup. it's delicious.

436
00:51:44.564 --> 00:51:46.899
Look mom. here comes the airplane.

437
00:52:20.725 --> 00:52:22.560
Oliver. there's someone outside!

438
00:52:22.643 --> 00:52:24.645
Take them downstairs.
fast run. run. run!

439
00:52:24.896 --> 00:52:26.230
Run. run!

440
00:53:06.521 --> 00:53:08.356
- Who else is in the house?
- Nobody!

441
00:53:08.397 --> 00:53:09.565
- Who?
- Nobody!

442
00:53:09.607 --> 00:53:11.566
- My parents went out.
- What about those screams?

443
00:53:11.567 --> 00:53:13.903
- We were...
- Hey. hey don't move.

444
00:53:17.990 --> 00:53:20.576
We were in the middle of Christmas dinner.

445
00:53:40.221 --> 00:53:41.556
Do you have water?

446
00:53:58.614 --> 00:53:59.740
Give it to me.

447
00:54:07.999 --> 00:54:10.334
Is there dessert? Chocolate?

448
00:54:11.377 --> 00:54:12.712
A cigarette?

449
00:54:22.972 --> 00:54:24.724
Fuck yes.

450
00:54:36.569 --> 00:54:38.404
Who knew cigarettes expire?

451
00:54:38.654 --> 00:54:41.324
All I have found are either dry or rancid.

452
00:54:41.657 --> 00:54:43.159
But whatever.

453
00:54:44.327 --> 00:54:45.369
Tobacco is tobacco.

454
00:54:47.038 --> 00:54:48.623
Where did your parents go?

455
00:54:49.040 --> 00:54:50.500
They went looking for food.

456
00:54:51.167 --> 00:54:52.293
How long ago?

457
00:54:52.668 --> 00:54:54.837
Why do you have an eye
with a different color?

458
00:54:57.882 --> 00:54:59.467
Because I'm a witch.

459
00:55:04.138 --> 00:55:06.182
I saw you in the woods.
sorry if I scared you.

460
00:55:06.224 --> 00:55:07.725
I just wanted to see what you had.

461
00:55:08.392 --> 00:55:11.479
I found the map in your backpack and came.

462
00:55:12.063 --> 00:55:13.815
The radio got screwed because of the water.

463
00:55:18.277 --> 00:55:20.363
Who are the people hanging outside?

464
00:55:22.657 --> 00:55:24.408
They lived here before.

465
00:55:24.575 --> 00:55:25.910
Who hung them?

466
00:55:26.077 --> 00:55:27.662
- My dad did.
- Did he...?

467
00:55:27.787 --> 00:55:30.414
No. they were like that
when we got here.

468
00:55:31.749 --> 00:55:32.750
Take them down.

469
00:55:32.792 --> 00:55:35.127
They attract too much attention.
Halloween is over.

470
00:55:35.461 --> 00:55:37.421
These windows must also be covered.

471
00:55:38.673 --> 00:55:41.175
The decoration of this place is... curious.

472
00:55:43.636 --> 00:55:45.179
Have you seen a plane around here?

473
00:55:45.805 --> 00:55:47.306
Or have you heard them?

474
00:55:47.723 --> 00:55:50.351
They're Russian.
they have the Red Cross.

475
00:55:50.768 --> 00:55:53.146
They fly around the world
dropping cold boxes with the cure.

476
00:55:53.187 --> 00:55:54.230
Medicine?

477
00:55:54.272 --> 00:55:55.439
A vaccine?

478
00:55:56.274 --> 00:55:57.984
You see. I told you.

479
00:55:59.318 --> 00:56:00.486
There’s a cure?

480
00:56:00.862 --> 00:56:03.906
A serum. Hyperimmune Gamma Globulin.

481
00:56:04.949 --> 00:56:08.828
It reverses the symptoms of the virus
and avoids contagion.

482
00:56:09.787 --> 00:56:11.372
I don't believe a damn thing.

483
00:56:11.497 --> 00:56:15.168
The world went to shit
because of a poorly tested vaccine.

484
00:56:15.710 --> 00:56:16.794
How do they drop them?

485
00:56:16.961 --> 00:56:18.045
With parachutes.

486
00:56:19.005 --> 00:56:21.048
They had to find it sooner or later.
right?

487
00:56:21.507 --> 00:56:24.302
The bad news is they
rarely fly over this area anymore.

488
00:56:24.343 --> 00:56:25.887
The way I see it.
we have two options.

489
00:56:25.928 --> 00:56:27.138
Option number one.

490
00:56:27.180 --> 00:56:31.350
We stay in this house. with the garden.
with all this. but without the cure.

491
00:56:31.559 --> 00:56:32.852
Option number two.

492
00:56:32.894 --> 00:56:36.397
We go out looking for the cure.
risk ourselves to find the best.

493
00:56:36.939 --> 00:56:37.982
"We" stay?

494
00:56:39.358 --> 00:56:40.776
Any fire trumpets nearby?

495
00:56:43.237 --> 00:56:44.363
We haven't come across them.

496
00:56:44.405 --> 00:56:48.659
We've only seen their tracks.
I'm sorry but you can't stay.

497
00:56:48.993 --> 00:56:51.120
The trumpets killed
everyone in my group.

498
00:56:52.622 --> 00:56:54.123
What are the trumpets?

499
00:56:54.749 --> 00:56:56.751
Those are real monsters?

500
00:56:59.504 --> 00:57:00.880
Want to watch a movie?

501
00:57:02.006 --> 00:57:03.549
How do you watch it?

502
00:57:06.093 --> 00:57:08.763
Are you kidding me?
It works without electricity?

503
00:57:09.013 --> 00:57:11.053
Can we watch a movie?
What other movies do you have?

504
00:57:11.641 --> 00:57:13.059
Just that one.

505
00:57:13.559 --> 00:57:15.686
One movie and one record.

506
00:57:18.481 --> 00:57:19.773
You can't stay here.

507
00:57:19.774 --> 00:57:22.151
If my parents come and see you.
they won't like it.

508
00:57:23.486 --> 00:57:25.029
Listen. Santiago.

509
00:57:26.072 --> 00:57:28.699
- Salvador.
- Salvador. nice to meet you. I'm Valeria.

510
00:57:30.618 --> 00:57:32.870
You're not going to let me go right now.
right?

511
00:57:33.162 --> 00:57:34.163
At night.

512
00:57:34.497 --> 00:57:37.583
It's dangerous. It's cold. I'm tired.

513
00:57:37.834 --> 00:57:39.752
It's been months since
I've talked to someone.

514
00:57:39.794 --> 00:57:41.921
And years since I watched a movie.

515
00:57:42.338 --> 00:57:43.422
Please.

516
00:57:50.012 --> 00:57:51.472
If you call that a movie.

517
00:57:51.514 --> 00:57:52.515
Yes!

518
00:57:52.557 --> 00:57:53.724
Who's going to play it?

519
00:58:24.881 --> 00:58:27.550
What were they smoking
when they made this movie?

520
00:58:39.604 --> 00:58:41.230
I'm sorry. I can't go any longer.

521
00:58:41.272 --> 00:58:43.399
Oliver. to your room. Take him!

522
00:58:43.566 --> 00:58:45.443
Okay. let's go.

523
00:58:49.989 --> 00:58:51.199
Good night.

524
00:58:54.869 --> 00:58:56.329
I was enjoying it.

525
00:58:58.456 --> 00:58:59.457
Thanks.

526
00:58:59.749 --> 00:59:02.168
It's the coolest thing
anyone has done for me in a long time.

527
00:59:02.335 --> 00:59:03.920
Since before all this started.

528
00:59:05.129 --> 00:59:07.423
No one ever rode a bike so I could
watch a movie.

529
00:59:09.091 --> 00:59:12.303
Not to mention someone with only one leg.

530
00:59:12.887 --> 00:59:14.096
No offense.

531
00:59:15.223 --> 00:59:16.349
What about that bike?

532
00:59:17.225 --> 00:59:19.977
My dad made it. he was an engineer.

533
00:59:21.103 --> 00:59:22.188
He was?

534
00:59:23.648 --> 00:59:24.649
He is.

535
00:59:24.816 --> 00:59:26.150
I helped him.

536
00:59:26.526 --> 00:59:27.819
What about your mother?

537
00:59:28.444 --> 00:59:29.904
She's a nurse.

538
00:59:31.697 --> 00:59:33.866
An engineer and a nurse!

539
00:59:34.116 --> 00:59:37.078
Damn! You and your
brothers really got lucky!

540
00:59:40.248 --> 00:59:41.499
What happened to you?

541
00:59:45.169 --> 00:59:46.963
I'm going to bed.
I'll get you some blankets.

542
00:59:47.129 --> 00:59:48.256
No. wait. huh?

543
00:59:53.261 --> 00:59:54.387
I want to take a bath.

544
00:59:56.347 --> 00:59:57.390
May I?

545
01:00:02.687 --> 01:00:04.147
Is that magazine good?

546
01:00:15.408 --> 01:00:17.076
Can I borrow a shirt or what?

547
01:00:41.767 --> 01:00:43.311
Thanks for heating the water.

548
01:00:47.648 --> 01:00:48.941
It was delicious.

549
01:01:11.547 --> 01:01:12.882
What do we have here?

550
01:01:17.345 --> 01:01:19.722
You know I've never been with a virgin?

551
01:01:21.182 --> 01:01:22.225
What?

552
01:01:23.935 --> 01:01:25.978
I want to pay you
for what you've done for me.

553
01:01:26.896 --> 01:01:28.147
Let me do it.

554
01:01:30.983 --> 01:01:33.569
When was the last time you saw a girl?

555
01:01:37.114 --> 01:01:38.533
Exactly.

556
01:01:45.540 --> 01:01:50.670
I haven't had many opportunities. either.

557
01:01:53.714 --> 01:01:57.885
Besides. it's easy and delicious.

558
01:01:59.804 --> 01:02:01.389
Like wanking?

559
01:02:01.889 --> 01:02:03.808
Much more.

560
01:02:06.978 --> 01:02:08.563
I can stay with you.

561
01:02:09.939 --> 01:02:11.816
We can talk to your parents.

562
01:02:14.735 --> 01:02:16.487
We have to repopulate the world. right?

563
01:02:18.030 --> 01:02:19.699
Two extra hands might be useful.

564
01:02:27.999 --> 01:02:31.043
We're fine. we don't need your help.

565
01:02:33.379 --> 01:02:34.422
Why?

566
01:02:37.049 --> 01:02:40.970
Why don't you share with those of us
who are also trying to survive?

567
01:02:42.346 --> 01:02:44.932
You don't know how things are
outside.

568
01:02:45.641 --> 01:02:47.143
With the infected.

569
01:02:48.060 --> 01:02:49.228
The trumpets.

570
01:02:58.613 --> 01:02:59.947
Well.

571
01:03:01.240 --> 01:03:02.825
Just for tonight.

572
01:03:06.829 --> 01:03:08.706
Should I turn off the lights?

573
01:03:52.959 --> 01:03:55.503
That was incredible.

574
01:03:55.795 --> 01:03:57.171
Thanks.

575
01:04:05.596 --> 01:04:07.974
I know you've had a very hard time
like everyone.

576
01:04:08.850 --> 01:04:10.393
but you can't stay.

577
01:04:11.018 --> 01:04:12.145
Forgive me.

578
01:04:17.483 --> 01:04:19.944
Hold me until dawn.
Then you won't see me again.

579
01:04:50.099 --> 01:04:51.476
Let's go.

580
01:04:51.642 --> 01:04:55.146
Oliver. take your brother and lock up!

581
01:04:55.188 --> 01:04:56.665
No! What's going to
happen to Salvador?

582
01:04:56.689 --> 01:04:57.982
Oliver!

583
01:04:58.316 --> 01:05:00.401
Take your brother and lock yourselves!

584
01:05:02.737 --> 01:05:03.863
On the table!

585
01:05:09.577 --> 01:05:11.370
Alcohol. quick!

586
01:05:14.499 --> 01:05:15.708
Alcohol!

587
01:05:17.251 --> 01:05:18.586
You are not gonna die!

588
01:05:20.505 --> 01:05:22.798
I'm sorry honey!

589
01:05:23.466 --> 01:05:24.550
I have to do it!

590
01:05:24.592 --> 01:05:27.428
I'm sorry! Don't move. dammit!

591
01:05:27.470 --> 01:05:28.554
Mom. am I going to die?

592
01:05:28.638 --> 01:05:29.639
Don't move!

593
01:05:30.473 --> 01:05:32.141
I'm gonna die!

594
01:05:34.477 --> 01:05:35.978
You're not gonna die!

595
01:05:36.145 --> 01:05:37.188
Calm down!

596
01:05:37.647 --> 01:05:39.190
Look at me. look at me!

597
01:05:39.315 --> 01:05:41.651
- Trust me. trust me.
- No dad. no!

598
01:05:42.235 --> 01:05:43.277
Bite. bite hard.

599
01:05:43.402 --> 01:05:45.738
- Bite hard!
- I'm sorry!

600
01:05:45.947 --> 01:05:46.989
Bite hard!

601
01:05:47.824 --> 01:05:48.866
I have to do it!

602
01:05:50.368 --> 01:05:52.286
Hold on. hold on!

603
01:05:55.706 --> 01:05:57.041
Hold him!

604
01:06:30.575 --> 01:06:33.995
No. no!

605
01:08:30.403 --> 01:08:31.571
Ah!

606
01:08:34.532 --> 01:08:35.616
Ah!

607
01:08:48.086 --> 01:08:50.213
An infected? Do you keep an infected here?

608
01:08:50.214 --> 01:08:52.133
You damn idiot. there are two kids here!

609
01:08:53.843 --> 01:08:55.010
Ah!

610
01:08:56.179 --> 01:08:58.430
No. no. no!

611
01:08:59.390 --> 01:09:01.184
Get off! Get off!

612
01:09:02.852 --> 01:09:04.769
Ah!

613
01:09:06.272 --> 01:09:07.523
Leave her!

614
01:10:01.536 --> 01:10:02.870
What was she doing there?

615
01:10:04.747 --> 01:10:07.082
Where did she get the keys to go
down there?

616
01:10:09.710 --> 01:10:11.128
What do we do with her body?

617
01:10:11.337 --> 01:10:13.047
We can use it as fertilizer
for the garden.

618
01:10:13.130 --> 01:10:15.424
It’s no good! It’s infected!

619
01:10:16.175 --> 01:10:18.052
There’s only one thing to do.

620
01:10:24.559 --> 01:10:27.228
Won't you say a few words or something?

621
01:10:33.985 --> 01:10:37.572
What do you want me to say?
I let my guard down. like an idiot.

622
01:10:39.073 --> 01:10:41.450
It won't happen to me
ever again.

623
01:11:25.286 --> 01:11:27.580
They loved that girl's meat.

624
01:11:28.289 --> 01:11:30.833
They've been eating
dogs and rats for a long time.

625
01:11:31.083 --> 01:11:32.793
Look at them now.

626
01:11:33.294 --> 01:11:34.629
We have to give them more.

627
01:11:34.837 --> 01:11:35.922
Give them more?

628
01:11:36.088 --> 01:11:38.758
Do you want them to be stronger?
We can barely control them.

629
01:11:42.428 --> 01:11:44.972
No diet change. are we clear?

630
01:12:05.409 --> 01:12:06.744
Are we sure about this?

631
01:12:07.662 --> 01:12:09.705
This house is the highest point in miles.

632
01:12:10.498 --> 01:12:12.124
What if the wrong people see it?

633
01:12:12.500 --> 01:12:14.168
Imagine if it does work.

634
01:12:14.585 --> 01:12:17.879
Imagine if the cure falls on us.
to be immune to the virus and above all...

635
01:12:17.880 --> 01:12:20.258
To be able to cure mom and dad.

636
01:13:11.142 --> 01:13:12.185
Mom.

637
01:13:12.727 --> 01:13:15.688
Mom. eat this!

638
01:13:17.023 --> 01:13:18.191
It’s meat!

639
01:13:19.317 --> 01:13:20.568
Just as you like it.

640
01:13:22.278 --> 01:13:23.278
Dad.

641
01:13:23.446 --> 01:13:24.697
It's meat. it's going to rot!

642
01:13:25.406 --> 01:13:26.406
Dad!

643
01:13:26.657 --> 01:13:27.657
Eat!

644
01:13:33.039 --> 01:13:34.790
So many years looking after them.

645
01:13:35.041 --> 01:13:38.669
Looking after ourselves.
Hiding them. feeding them.

646
01:13:38.961 --> 01:13:40.004
For what?

647
01:13:40.171 --> 01:13:42.715
What’s the point of keeping them
in this suffering?

648
01:13:44.050 --> 01:13:45.551
What's the point of educating them?

649
01:13:46.511 --> 01:13:48.137
What fucking life is this?

650
01:13:50.807 --> 01:13:55.394
Benjamin insists on the same.
he wants to give them Valeria's body.

651
01:13:56.604 --> 01:13:57.730
What do you think?

652
01:13:59.232 --> 01:14:03.194
I want them to be okay.
but I'm still afraid of them.

653
01:14:05.404 --> 01:14:06.864
Don't worry.

654
01:14:07.198 --> 01:14:10.076
I'll make sure he doesn't do anything
stupid.

655
01:14:28.761 --> 01:14:30.512
Why don't you ever listen?

656
01:14:30.513 --> 01:14:32.098
Don't you trust my decisions?

657
01:14:32.890 --> 01:14:33.932
What will you do?

658
01:14:33.933 --> 01:14:35.309
Don’t fucking ask.

659
01:14:38.729 --> 01:14:41.524
Bugger off or cover your nose.

660
01:14:41.983 --> 01:14:43.025
No!

661
01:15:18.728 --> 01:15:24.233
“Once upon a time. there were
two children named Hansel and Gretel.

662
01:15:24.567 --> 01:15:31.574
Who lived with their father. a lumberjack.
and their stepmother near a dense forest”.

663
01:15:32.450 --> 01:15:35.661
“The family's situation was precarious.

664
01:15:36.162 --> 01:15:41.667
They lived with scarcity and barely
had enough to eat”.

665
01:15:42.335 --> 01:15:44.295
- Benja.
- You shut up!

666
01:15:50.760 --> 01:15:53.596
"One night. the cruel stepmother"...

667
01:15:53.971 --> 01:15:55.473
We have to give them something else.

668
01:15:55.556 --> 01:15:58.059
I offered them everything
we have but they don't want it.

669
01:15:58.142 --> 01:16:00.478
I told you we had to give them the body.

670
01:16:00.937 --> 01:16:02.104
Maybe it's the best for them.

671
01:16:02.563 --> 01:16:04.357
At least that way they'll stop suffering.

672
01:16:04.482 --> 01:16:05.733
What are you talking about?

673
01:16:05.942 --> 01:16:07.235
What else do you want to do?

674
01:16:07.777 --> 01:16:09.445
Valeria's meat was good for them.

675
01:16:10.404 --> 01:16:12.114
You want to kill to feed them?

676
01:16:13.032 --> 01:16:14.200
We are not murderers.

677
01:16:14.367 --> 01:16:17.012
You don't care about the cure
because you don't care about mom and dad!

678
01:16:17.036 --> 01:16:18.704
You only care about your fucking rules!

679
01:16:18.746 --> 01:16:20.664
You don't believe they are people!

680
01:16:20.665 --> 01:16:22.375
They are not people. Benjamin!

681
01:16:22.750 --> 01:16:24.919
People are those who are out there
in the real world.

682
01:16:25.044 --> 01:16:26.879
if you kill them. you're a murderer.

683
01:16:27.171 --> 01:16:28.172
We kill dogs.

684
01:16:28.297 --> 01:16:29.423
It's not the same.

685
01:16:29.465 --> 01:16:30.675
Don't be stupid.

686
01:16:30.716 --> 01:16:32.802
Besides. tell me who is going to do it?

687
01:16:33.427 --> 01:16:35.304
You. Benjamin?
You can't even kill a fly.

688
01:16:35.388 --> 01:16:38.307
You. Oliver?
You can't even skin a fucking dead dog.

689
01:16:38.474 --> 01:16:42.102
They are our parents!
You want them to die!

690
01:16:42.103 --> 01:16:45.022
What I want is to save our family!

691
01:16:45.314 --> 01:16:47.108
I'm not going to argue anymore.

692
01:16:47.441 --> 01:16:50.736
You will not leave until the three of us
agree on what to do.

693
01:16:51.571 --> 01:16:52.738
Let's vote!

694
01:16:54.157 --> 01:16:57.784
Those who want to... hunt for... food
for mom and dad

695
01:16:57.785 --> 01:16:59.078
raise your hand.

696
01:17:09.255 --> 01:17:10.756
Those who want to let them die.

697
01:17:17.013 --> 01:17:18.431
Do whatever the fuck you want.

698
01:17:18.472 --> 01:17:20.308
I want to see who kills who.

699
01:17:23.978 --> 01:17:25.563
The ground is too hard.

700
01:17:25.855 --> 01:17:28.191
Why don't we just use Guillermina?

701
01:17:28.441 --> 01:17:30.818
To kill someone with Guillermina
you need to be very close.

702
01:17:33.029 --> 01:17:34.405
How much are we going to dig?

703
01:17:34.489 --> 01:17:35.490
I don't know.

704
01:17:35.615 --> 01:17:36.895
What do you mean you don't know?

705
01:17:39.535 --> 01:17:40.620
That's a lot.

706
01:17:41.204 --> 01:17:43.206
It has to be deep enough.
so it can't get out.

707
01:17:43.581 --> 01:17:45.208
Then how do we get it out?

708
01:17:45.666 --> 01:17:46.709
With a rope.

709
01:17:46.876 --> 01:17:47.960
Who is going to tie it?

710
01:17:48.085 --> 01:17:49.170
Between the two of us.

711
01:17:49.420 --> 01:17:51.589
And how are we going to get out?

712
01:19:54.378 --> 01:19:58.007
"One night. the cruel stepmother
suggested to the good lumberjack

713
01:19:58.049 --> 01:20:02.136
who was suffering thinking
that his children were starving".

714
01:20:03.221 --> 01:20:05.139
"We must abandon them in the forest".

715
01:20:05.681 --> 01:20:07.558
"There's not enough food".

716
01:20:07.600 --> 01:20:10.812
"Maybe someone will find them.
take pity and feed them".

717
01:20:11.270 --> 01:20:15.607
"At first. the father was adamantly opposed
to the idea of abandoning

718
01:20:15.608 --> 01:20:17.610
his children to the mercy of the forest".

719
01:20:24.742 --> 01:20:26.410
Wake up you lazy bastards.

720
01:20:26.828 --> 01:20:28.913
Are you ready to build an awesome trap?

721
01:20:35.002 --> 01:20:38.840
That's how it has to look. Just add
some more leaves to cover the planks.

722
01:20:39.340 --> 01:20:40.383
Any questions?

723
01:20:40.675 --> 01:20:42.051
Hold this.

724
01:20:43.636 --> 01:20:44.971
Here is a military checkpoint.

725
01:20:45.346 --> 01:20:47.181
Where Benjamin and I saw clothes hanging.

726
01:20:48.099 --> 01:20:50.810
All this is forest.

727
01:20:52.478 --> 01:20:55.064
On your way back.
the sun has to be on your left.

728
01:20:55.106 --> 01:20:57.483
Also behind you in the afternoon.

729
01:21:00.403 --> 01:21:02.488
Without the radios
I can't help you at all.

730
01:21:02.572 --> 01:21:04.490
If you get lost. you're on your own.

731
01:21:05.700 --> 01:21:07.368
If you see the trumpets

732
01:21:07.410 --> 01:21:10.496
or some other infected. run!

733
01:21:11.330 --> 01:21:12.540
Understood?

734
01:23:56.412 --> 01:23:58.956
That's how mom and dad would end
if we don't feed them.

735
01:24:00.208 --> 01:24:01.918
What are we going to do?

736
01:24:06.130 --> 01:24:07.131
Hurry up.

737
01:24:17.683 --> 01:24:20.228
I think this is where Salvador pointed.

738
01:24:33.324 --> 01:24:35.743
Come. let's set the camp.

739
01:25:11.571 --> 01:25:13.197
Hey. let me look too.

740
01:25:17.076 --> 01:25:18.411
Come. let's go.

741
01:25:39.140 --> 01:25:40.183
Help!

742
01:25:40.641 --> 01:25:42.977
Somebody help me. please!

743
01:25:44.479 --> 01:25:45.980
Help!

744
01:25:54.614 --> 01:25:55.865
Help!

745
01:25:56.657 --> 01:25:57.992
It hurts a lot!

746
01:25:59.160 --> 01:26:00.160
It hurts me!

747
01:26:02.038 --> 01:26:03.247
Help me!

748
01:26:04.790 --> 01:26:06.125
Help!

749
01:26:08.461 --> 01:26:09.670
Help me!

750
01:26:10.338 --> 01:26:12.298
Someone help me please!

751
01:26:23.518 --> 01:26:24.727
What are you doing here kid?

752
01:26:25.436 --> 01:26:26.562
I got lost.

753
01:26:30.983 --> 01:26:32.151
Who’s with you?

754
01:26:33.861 --> 01:26:35.071
I'm alone.

755
01:26:39.951 --> 01:26:40.952
Were you bitten?

756
01:26:44.872 --> 01:26:46.374
Answer me! Were you bitten?

757
01:26:46.791 --> 01:26:47.875
Ah!

758
01:26:49.752 --> 01:26:50.752
Calm down.

759
01:26:50.753 --> 01:26:52.380
I'm going to help you.

760
01:27:15.862 --> 01:27:18.239
Stupid kids. what do you want?

761
01:27:24.453 --> 01:27:26.038
Shit. what do you want?

762
01:27:29.584 --> 01:27:31.169
You're going to kill me?

763
01:27:31.836 --> 01:27:32.837
Huh?

764
01:27:34.005 --> 01:27:36.465
You're going to shoot me like an infected?

765
01:27:38.384 --> 01:27:40.094
Look me in the eyes. you bastard!

766
01:27:41.304 --> 01:27:42.430
Kill me.

767
01:27:44.140 --> 01:27:45.391
Are you scared?

768
01:27:46.392 --> 01:27:47.393
Kill me!

769
01:27:47.768 --> 01:27:49.520
Shoot here!

770
01:27:50.354 --> 01:27:54.400
Shoot asshole. if you're going to kill me.
look me in the eye!

771
01:27:54.901 --> 01:27:55.985
Look me in the eye!

772
01:28:04.202 --> 01:28:05.912
You wanted to kill me. asshole?

773
01:28:05.953 --> 01:28:07.121
Let me go!

774
01:29:40.256 --> 01:29:42.049
Quick. Let's go.
Don't look back.

775
01:30:00.276 --> 01:30:01.277
Congratulations.

776
01:30:01.319 --> 01:30:02.361
You did it.

777
01:30:02.653 --> 01:30:04.280
I'm proud of you.

778
01:30:05.698 --> 01:30:07.325
But this is just the beginning.

779
01:31:13.891 --> 01:31:15.726
- What is it?
- No idea.

780
01:31:16.853 --> 01:31:17.937
Should we go out?

781
01:31:19.021 --> 01:31:20.439
What if it's a plane?

782
01:31:21.440 --> 01:31:23.568
Planes don't sound like that.

783
01:31:23.943 --> 01:31:25.027
Go to your room.

784
01:31:25.444 --> 01:31:26.737
I'll stay here watching.

785
01:32:10.990 --> 01:32:13.075
I brought you water.
a guava. and a blanket.

786
01:32:13.784 --> 01:32:15.369
Tomorrow we'll take a walk.

787
01:32:15.620 --> 01:32:17.330
You and Benjamin sleep in the basement.

788
01:32:53.324 --> 01:32:54.659
Hide. hide. fast!

789
01:33:01.249 --> 01:33:02.124
Go away or I'll shoot!

790
01:33:02.166 --> 01:33:04.460
I'm not here to steal or harm anyone.

791
01:33:04.961 --> 01:33:06.045
I just want to hide.

792
01:33:06.087 --> 01:33:07.213
Go away or I'll shoot!

793
01:33:07.255 --> 01:33:11.509
Only the Almighty knows
when and where my life will end.

794
01:33:12.051 --> 01:33:14.554
I'd rather die from a bullet
than getting caught.

795
01:33:15.263 --> 01:33:16.347
Infected?

796
01:33:16.389 --> 01:33:18.266
No. worse.

797
01:33:28.067 --> 01:33:30.027
But it’s only children!

798
01:33:30.570 --> 01:33:31.946
- Innocents!
- Hey. hey. hey!

799
01:33:32.196 --> 01:33:33.406
Not one more step I said.

800
01:33:34.073 --> 01:33:35.116
Who are they?

